        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Inclusion–exclusion (I-E) is the correction machine of counting: when sets\noverlap, you cannot just add. **Add the singletons, subtract the pairwise\noverlaps, add back the triples, and alternate.** The complement form — *count the\nelements satisfying none of a list of \"bad\" properties* — is the version you\nactually reach for, because most counting problems are \"how many avoid all of\nthese forbidden conditions.\""
    },
