      "text": "## Layer 1 — The Principle, Two Forms"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#006",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   UNION FORM\n   | A_1 u ... u A_n | = SUM_{k=1}^{n} (-1)^{k+1}\n                          SUM_{|S|=k} | A_{i1} INTERSECT ... INTERSECT A_{ik} |"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#007",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COMPLEMENT FORM (more useful)\n   Let U = universe, A_i = \"elements WITH bad property i\".\n   # elements with NO bad property =\n        SUM_{S subset of [n]} (-1)^{|S|} | A_S |\n   where A_S = INTERSECT_{i in S} A_i  and  A_empty = U.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#008",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Why the alternating signs work.** Take an element `x` with *exactly* `m` of the\nbad properties. Its net contribution to the complement-form sum is\n`Σ_{j=0}^{m} (-1)^j C(m,j)`, the number of size-S subsets among its `m`\nproperties weighted by sign. By the alternating binomial identity (`02`), this is\n`0` for `m ≥ 1` and `1` for `m = 0`. So every element with at least one bad\nproperty cancels to zero, and only the \"clean\" elements survive — exactly what\nthe complement form claims. The proof *is* the `Σ (-1)^j C(m,j) = [m=0]` identity."
    },
    {
