      },
      "text": "## Layer 2 — Derangements (the flagship application)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#011",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A **derangement** is a permutation with no fixed point: `π(i) ≠ i` for all `i`.\n\"How many ways can n hats be returned so nobody gets their own?\""
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#012",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   Universe U = all n! permutations.\n   Bad property i = \"fixes point i\" (pi(i) = i).\n   A_S = permutations fixing every i in S = (n - |S|)! arrangements\n         of the remaining points.  There are C(n,|S|) sets of each size."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#013",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "D_n = SUM_{j=0}^{n} (-1)^j C(n,j) (n-j)!\n       = n! SUM_{j=0}^{n} (-1)^j / j!\n       = n! * [ 1 - 1 + 1/2! - 1/3! + ... ]\n       ->  n!/e   as n -> infinity."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#014",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "D_0=1, D_1=0, D_2=1, D_3=2, D_4=9, D_5=44, ...\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#015",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The punchline is striking: `D_n / n! → 1/e ≈ 0.3679`. The **probability a random\npermutation is a derangement converges to 1/e**, essentially independent of `n`.\nThere is also a clean recurrence `D_n = (n-1)(D_{n-1} + D_{n-2})`, and the EGF\n(`03`) is `e^{-x}/(1-x)` — the `e^{-x}` is the I-E sign-alternation, `1/(1-x)`\nthe `n!`."
    },
