      },
      "text": "## Layer 4 — The Sieve and Number-Theoretic I-E"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#026",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Inclusion–exclusion *is* the abstract sieve; the **sieve of Eratosthenes** and\nEuler's totient are its number-theory incarnations (full treatment in\n`number-theory/`)."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#027",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   EULER'S TOTIENT phi(n) = # integers in [1,n] coprime to n.\n   For n = p1^a1 ... pr^ar, \"bad property i\" = divisible by p_i."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#028",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "phi(n) = SUM_{S subset of {p1..pr}} (-1)^{|S|} * n / (PROD_{p in S} p)\n          = n PROD_{i=1}^{r} (1 - 1/p_i)."
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#029",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Example n = 12 = 2^2 * 3:\n   phi(12) = 12 (1 - 1/2)(1 - 1/3) = 12 * 1/2 * 2/3 = 4.\n   ({1,5,7,11} -- the four coprime residues.)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md#030",
      "path": [
        "04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion, git-history:combinatorics:04-inclusion-exclusion]",
        "canonical_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion, derangements, surjections, sieve, bonferroni]",
        "current_path": "combinatorics/04-INCLUSION-EXCLUSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:combinatorics:inclusion-exclusion",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "combinatorics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[inclusion-exclusion]",
        "section": "combinatorics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Inclusion-Exclusion and the Sieve",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "This is I-E with the universe `{1,...,n}` and bad properties \"divisible by\nprime `p_i`.\" The product form `∏(1 - 1/p)` is exactly the alternating sum\nfactored — multiplicativity of `φ` falls out for free. The general \"count\nintegers up to N divisible by none of a set of primes\" is the **Legendre sieve**,\nthe analytic-number-theory workhorse (`number-theory/07`)."
    }
